.TH LANCHESS 6 "2026-10-01" "lanchess 1.0.0" "Games"
.SH NAME
lanchess \- terminal chess for two players on the same network
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY lanchess
.B host
.OP \-\-port N
.OP \-\-name NAME
.OP \-\-color white|black|random
.OP \-\-time TC
.OP \-\-fen FEN
.OP \-\-no\-discovery
.RI [ common-options ]
.YS
.SY lanchess
.B join
.RI [ HOST [: PORT ]]
.OP \-\-port N
.OP \-\-name NAME
.OP \-\-scan\-time S
.RI [ common-options ]
.YS
.SY lanchess
.B local
.OP \-\-time TC
.OP \-\-fen FEN
.OP \-\-no\-flip
.RI [ common-options ]
.YS
.SY lanchess
.B \-\-version
.YS
.PP
.I common-options
are
.OP \-\-ascii
.OP \-\-no\-color
.OP \-\-plain
.OP \-\-pgn\-dir DIR
.OP \-\-no\-save
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lanchess
plays chess inside a terminal.
Two people on two computers on the same Wi\-Fi or wired network play
against each other: one computer
.BR host s
the game, the other
.BR join s
it.
There is also a hot\-seat mode,
.BR local ,
for two players sharing one keyboard.
.PP
The screen shows a live board, chess clocks, captured pieces, the move list,
a message log with chat, and an input line.
Draw offers, takebacks and rematches are supported, and every finished game
is saved as a PGN file.
.PP
.B lanchess
uses only the Python standard library and needs Python 3.8 or newer.
Both players must run the same protocol version.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B host
Listen for an opponent on TCP port 5555 (or
.BR \-\-port ).
The host prints its IP addresses together with the exact
.B join
command to type on the other computer, answers network searches on
UDP port 5556, and waits until an opponent connects.
Press Ctrl\-C to stop waiting.
The host's colour, time control and start position apply to both players.
.TP
.BR join " [\fIHOST\fR[:\fIPORT\fR]]"
Connect to a host.
.I HOST
is an IP address such as
.B 192.168.1.23
or a host name, optionally followed by a colon and a port number
.RB ( 192.168.1.23:6000 ).
Without
.IR HOST ,
the network is searched for a few seconds and the games found are listed;
type the number of a game or an address.
.TP
.B local
Hot\-seat game on one computer.
Whoever is to move types the move, and the board turns to face the side to
move.
.B /draw
ends the game as a draw at once,
.B /resign
resigns for the side to move and
.B /takeback
undoes one move at once.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-port " N"
.BR host :
TCP port to listen on.
.BR join :
port to connect to when
.I HOST
has no
.BI : PORT
part.
Default: 5555.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
The name your opponent sees, trimmed to 20 characters.
Default: your login name, or
.BR Player .
.TP
.BR \-\-color " white|black|random"
.BR host :
the host's own colour; the joiner gets the other one.
Default: white.
.TP
.BI \-\-time " TC"
.BR host ", " local :
time control
.IB MINUTES + INCREMENT ,
for example
.B 5+3
(5 minutes each plus 3 seconds per move),
.B 10
(10 minutes, no increment) or
.B 0.5+0
(30 seconds).
.B none
or
.B 0
means untimed, which is the default.
No clock runs until White makes the first move.
.TP
.BI \-\-fen " FEN"
.BR host ", " local :
start from a custom position given in Forsyth\-Edwards Notation.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-discovery
.BR host :
do not answer network searches; the joiner must type the host's address.
.TP
.BI \-\-scan\-time " S"
.BR join :
how many seconds to search the network for hosts.
Default: 2.5.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-flip
.BR local :
keep the board facing one way instead of turning it to the side to move.
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
Draw pieces as letters (K Q R B N P) instead of chess symbols.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Turn off colours and all terminal escape sequences.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Line\-by\-line output instead of the full\-screen view, for basic terminals,
screen readers, logging or scripted input.
The board is printed after every change.
.TP
.BI \-\-pgn\-dir " DIR"
Directory for saved games.
Default:
.IR ~/lanchess_games/ .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-save
Do not save finished games automatically.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENTERING MOVES
Type a move and press Enter.
Standard algebraic notation
.RB ( e4 ", " Nf3 ", " exd5 ", " O\-O ", " e8=Q )
and coordinates
.RB ( e2e4 ", " e2\-e4 ", " g1f3 ", " e7e8q )
are both accepted, and capital letters are optional.
Castling may also be typed as
.BR 0\-0 ,
.B o\-o
or as the king moving two squares
.RB ( e1g1 ).
A pawn reaching the last rank becomes a queen unless another piece is named.
Anything that does not start with
.B /
is read as a move.
.SH IN-GAME COMMANDS
.TP
.BR /help ", " ?
Show the command reference.
.TP
.BR /c ", " /chat ", " /say " \fImessage\fR"
Send a chat message (up to 500 characters).
.TP
.B /resign
Resign the game.
.TP
.B /draw
Offer a draw, or accept the opponent's offer.
.TP
.BR /accept ", " /decline
Answer the opponent's pending draw, takeback or rematch offer.
.TP
.BR /takeback ", " /undo
Ask to take back your last move.
.TP
.B /flip
Turn the board around.
.TP
.B /moves
List the legal moves.
.TP
.B /fen
Show the current position as FEN.
.TP
.B /pgn
Show the game so far as PGN.
.TP
.BR /save " [\fIpath\fR]"
Save the game as PGN now, to
.I path
or to the default directory.
.TP
.B /rematch
After the game ends, offer a rematch with colours swapped.
.TP
.BR /quit ", " /exit ", " /q
Leave the program.
During a network game in progress the first
.B /quit
asks for confirmation; a second one within 10 seconds resigns and leaves.
.TP
.B /clear
Clear the message log.
.SH KEYS
In the full\-screen view: Up and Down recall earlier input;
Left, Right, Home, End, Ctrl\-A and Ctrl\-E move the cursor;
Ctrl\-U clears the input line; Ctrl\-W deletes the previous word;
PgUp and PgDn scroll the message log; Ctrl\-L redraws the screen.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/lanchess_games/
Finished games are saved here as
.IR YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS _ White -vs- Black .pgn
unless
.B \-\-no\-save
or
.B \-\-pgn\-dir
is given.
.TP
.I /usr/share/lanchess/
The Python package used by the
.B lanchess
command (under
.I /usr/local/share/lanchess/
for a
.B make install
with the default prefix).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/firewalld/services/lanchess.xml
firewalld service definition opening TCP 5555 and UDP 5556
.RI ( /etc/firewalld/services/lanchess.xml
after a
.B make install
with a prefix other than
.IR /usr ).
.TP
.I /etc/ufw/applications.d/lanchess
ufw application profile opening TCP 5555 and UDP 5556.
.SH NETWORK AND FIREWALL
The host must accept incoming
.B TCP port 5555
for the game (or the port given with
.BR \-\-port )
and
.B UDP port 5556
for network search.
The joining computer usually needs no changes.
Joining by IP address only needs the TCP port.
.PP
With firewalld:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo firewall\-cmd \-\-add\-service=lanchess
sudo firewall\-cmd \-\-permanent \-\-add\-service=lanchess
.EE
.RE
.PP
With ufw:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo ufw allow lanchess
.EE
.RE
.PP
Guest, hotel and public Wi\-Fi networks often isolate clients from each
other; LAN play cannot work on them.
.SH EXAMPLES
On the first computer:
.PP
.RS
.EX
lanchess host \-\-time 5+3
.EE
.RE
.PP
On the second computer, search the network or give the host's address:
.PP
.RS
.EX
lanchess join
lanchess join 192.168.1.23
.EE
.RE
.PP
A hot\-seat game with letters instead of symbols:
.PP
.RS
.EX
lanchess local \-\-ascii
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR firewall\-cmd (1),
.BR ufw (8)
.PP
Project page: https://github.com/DeveshB\-1/lanchess
